{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-216726",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, note that $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined.\n\nTo solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator $(2x-1)$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+4}{2x-1} & =5 \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot \\frac{7x+4}{2x-1} & =(2x-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\ \\cancel{(2x-1)}\\cdot \\frac{7x+4}{\\cancel{2x-1}} & =(2x-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\ 7x+4 & =10x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+4 & =10x-5 \\\\ 7x+4+5 & =10x-5+5 \\\\ 7x+9 & =10x \\\\ 7x+9-7x & =10x-7x \\\\ 9 & =3x \\\\ \\frac{9}{3} & =\\frac{3x}{3} \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=3$ is different from $x=\\frac{1}{2}$, we can accept it as a solution. Thus, the solution is $x=3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-216726\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>First, note that <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"86\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle space=\"4\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> cannot be a solution since division by <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"87\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is undefined.</p>\n<p>To solve the equation, we first multiply both sides by the denominator <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"88\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c